      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We studied the relation between angiographically defined coronary artery disease and serologic evidence of Helicobacter pylori infection in 488 patients undergo ing elective coronary angiography. There was no association between Helicobacter pylori infection and coronary artery disease (odds ratio 1.3, 95% confidence interval 0.83 to 2.16)."},
